242
00:14:31,030 --> 00:14:33,070
But she's really terrific.

243
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,280
It's too bad.

244
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,160
No, I'm saying I liked her.

245
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:41,290
There are other fish in the sea.

246
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,800
I think she's great, okay? We're going out again.

247
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:49,630
I hear you. Are you capable of talking about anything else?

248
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:53,470
Which one's my turkey burger?

249
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,970
The one next to my foot. Sorry.

250
00:14:56,970 --> 00:14:59,230
- Fight's starting!     - We'll be right in.

251
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:02,310
So did your boss try to slap you again today?

252
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,980
Nine times.

253
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:06,440
I had to put on lotion.

254
00:15:08,610 --> 00:15:11,490
But it'll be okay. Tomorrow, I conduct an experiment.

255
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:15,740
And if all goes as planned, my butt will be smack-free.

256
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:17,620
Fight's over!

257
00:15:23,210 --> 00:15:24,670
Excuse me, Doug?

258
00:15:27,090 --> 00:15:29,130
Hey there, sports fan!

259
00:15:29,510 --> 00:15:31,970
Bing! You got those numbers for me?

260
00:15:32,180 --> 00:15:34,090
No. I didn't do them.

261
00:15:34,350 --> 00:15:36,220
Oh. You forgot?

262
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:38,930
No, I just didn't do them.

263
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:42,850
Instead, I hung out with some friends and had a couple of beers.

264
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:45,810
So I certainly don't deserve praise. Verbal...

265
00:15:46,020 --> 00:15:47,650
...or otherwise.

266
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:51,360
I got tanked myself last night. Pretty dicey drive home.

267
00:15:51,610 --> 00:15:54,030
Tappan Zee Bridge never looked smaller. Ha, ha.

268
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:58,280
That's okay. You're still my number one guy! Bing!

269
00:15:58,870 --> 00:16:01,120
Doug!

270
00:16:01,290 --> 00:16:05,830
I'm a little bit uncomfortable with the way that you express yourself.

271
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:08,630
Is it the swearing? Is it the constant swearing?

272
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:12,840
Because I gotta tell you, if it is, you can just kiss my ass!

273
00:16:14,890 --> 00:16:17,640
No. It's not about the swearing. It's more about...

274
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:20,350
...the way that you occasionally...

275
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:24,060
...concentrate your enthusiasm...

276
00:16:25,350 --> 00:16:26,900
...on my buttocks.

277
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:32,280
Don't get me wrong, I appreciate the sentiment.

278
00:16:32,490 --> 00:16:36,320
It's just that I have a rather sensitive posterior.

279
00:16:38,160 --> 00:16:41,410
And besides, it's making all the other guys jealous.

280
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:45,670
Well, say no more. You know, it takes guts to bring this up.

281
00:16:45,920 --> 00:16:47,880
Bing, you're okay.

282
00:16:48,040 --> 00:16:49,090
Okay.

283
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,720
Would you rather live in the shirt pocket of a sweaty giant...

284
00:17:01,930 --> 00:17:04,430
...or inside his shower drain?

285
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,730
Oh, my God.

286
00:17:08,310 --> 00:17:10,360
Look. It's Ross and that girl.

287
00:17:13,690 --> 00:17:18,200
Look at that! It's a line of ants! They're working as a team!

288
00:17:20,200 --> 00:17:24,330
Right. Oh, yeah. It looks like Ross is breaking up with her.

289
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,040
I hope he lets her down easy.

290
00:17:26,290 --> 00:17:29,250
Look at that! They are not breaking up! Look at them!

291
00:17:29,460 --> 00:17:32,460
You know what that is? A second date, that's what that is.

292
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:35,470
Look, she just put her hand on his thigh.

293
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:38,300
That's nothing. She's very sexually aggressive.

294
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:39,590
Oh, God!

295
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:44,640
It's your fault. Now he loves her. He'll marry her. It's all your fault.

296
00:17:45,350 --> 00:17:46,850
You said it was okay.

297
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:49,230
You said she was bald!

298
00:17:50,650 --> 00:17:52,980
Was! Was, was, was!

299
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:58,320
We can't let it happen. We have to do something. We have to break them up.

300
00:17:58,570 --> 00:18:02,780
Just go in there and shave her head! You owe me one bald girl!

301
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:06,410
Okay, first of all, breathe.

302
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:10,000
Second of all, I don't get it.

303
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:13,460
Aren't you the one that decided you didn't want to be with Ross?

304
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:16,670
Yes.

305
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:20,640
Well, isn't he your friend? Don't you want him to be happy?

306
00:18:23,010 --> 00:18:24,010
Yes.

307
00:18:24,850 --> 00:18:26,020
So?

308
00:18:30,270 --> 00:18:34,770
It's just, you know, I didn't expect him to be this happy so soon.

309
00:18:44,450 --> 00:18:45,490
- Oh, no.     - What?

310
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:46,830
We killed them all!

311
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:05,930
It's not as bad as it looks. It's a precaution.

312
00:19:06,180 --> 00:19:08,680
I'm not supposed to move my spine.

313
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:13,060
Please tell me you're stopping now.

314
00:19:13,440 --> 00:19:16,190
I'm fine. I'd fight tonight if they'd let me.

315
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:20,490
Now, see this circle I'm marking off here?

316
00:19:20,700 --> 00:19:22,700
This is my Zone of Terror.

317
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:28,830
You are insane! You've got to give this up!

318
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:31,960
I can't until I'm the Ultimate Fighter.

319
00:19:32,170 --> 00:19:33,330
I will do it.

320
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:37,840
The day will come when children will argue over who will win a fight...

321
00:19:38,090 --> 00:19:40,010
...me or Superman.

322
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:44,890
Not that I could beat Superman, but kids are stupid.

323
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:47,390
Just sit down.

324
00:19:47,600 --> 00:19:49,470
Please listen to me.

325
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:54,690
You are terrible at this, okay? You are the worst Ultimate Fighter ever.

326
00:19:55,110 --> 00:19:56,110
Ever!

327
00:19:57,570 --> 00:20:01,610
I have a torn rotator cuff, a hairline fracture in my right forearm...

328
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:05,990
...and a severely bruised Adam's apple, but that really hurt.

329
00:20:11,620 --> 00:20:13,870
Well, then you know what?

330
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:20,090
I care about you too much to watch you hurt yourself like this.

331
00:20:20,590 --> 00:20:24,010
So if you have to do this, you'll have to do it without me.

332
00:20:24,510 --> 00:20:26,430
If you're asking me to quit...

333
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:29,510
...then you're asking me to be someone I'm not.

334
00:20:29,810 --> 00:20:31,270
I've got to do this.

335
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:37,440
Then I've gotta go.

336
00:20:39,190 --> 00:20:40,230
Bye.

337
00:20:46,030 --> 00:20:47,820
- Monica?     - Yes?

338
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,660
Could you leave a note? I'm on painkillers...

339
00:20:50,950 --> 00:20:53,080
...and I might not remember this tomorrow.

340
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:03,550
So, in conclusion, the lines all go up, so I'm happy.

341
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:06,760
Great job, team! Tomorrow at 8:30.

342
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:10,430
Phil, nice job! Stevens, way to go!

343
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,850
Goldberg, you maniac!

344
00:21:13,100 --> 00:21:14,680
I love you!

345
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:20,690
- Bing, couldn't have done it without you.     - Thank you, sir.

346
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:22,280
Oh, excuse me.

347
00:21:22,480 --> 00:21:26,200
I forgot my briefcase, you know, by accident.

348
00:21:26,490 --> 00:21:28,660
Of course you did. Forgot something else too, you bastard!

349
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,790
Well, what about you?

350
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:37,540
You're not feeling left out, are you?

351
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:41,460
No, not at all. That's ridiculous.

352
00:21:41,670 --> 00:21:44,880
Everybody else got one, and you want one too. Don't you?

353
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:49,550
Yes, I do.

354
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:51,970
Now, get on out of here, you!

355
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,810
Pete Becker circles the ring.

356
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:01,520
Looks like he's just trying to feel him out.

357
00:22:01,730 --> 00:22:03,230
Bruiser is charging!

358
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:06,150
Run, you crazy, rich freak!

359
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:09,070
I can't watch this.

360
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:10,990
Check it out! Pete's winning!

361
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:13,240
- Really?     - No!

362
00:22:15,750 --> 00:22:20,170
Uh-oh, Bruiser has Becker on the canvas and is going for his favorite area!

363
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:25,920
Wait! If that's his favorite area, why is he being so mean to it?

364
00:22:26,590 --> 00:22:27,840
This is ironic.

365
00:22:28,090 --> 00:22:30,760
Your last boyfriend, Richard, didn't want to have kids.

366
00:22:31,010 --> 00:22:33,600
And from the looks of it, now Pete can't.

